    "text": "Fast forward to today, and the dollar is still the king of world money. It makes up close to sixty percent of the world's foreign currency reserves, and it's on one side of nearly nine in every ten currency trades. That's what gives American sanctions their bite. Cut a country off from dollars, and you cut it off from most of the world economy. Just ask Iran, or Russia, which in twenty twenty two saw roughly three hundred billion dollars of its central bank reserves frozen almost overnight. And when the dollar gets stronger, every poorer country that borrowed in dollars suddenly owes more, without borrowing a single extra cent.",
